   "daf": "137b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "וְאִם הָיָה בַּעַל בָּשָׂר וְכוּ׳. אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: קָטָן הַמְסוּרְבָּל בְּבָשָׂר, רוֹאִין אוֹתוֹ, כׇּל זְמַן שֶׁמִּתְקַשֶּׁה וְנִרְאֶה מָהוּל — אֵינוֹ צָרִיךְ לָמוּל, וְאִם לָאו — צָרִיךְ לָמוּל.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «If» the baby «was fleshy,» the circumcisor corrects the circumcision so that it will not appear uncircumcised. «Shmuel said: A child who is encumbered with flesh, one examines him,» and «as long as when» his limb «hardens he looks circumcised, one need not circumcise» him again. «And if not,» meaning he does not appear circumcised even then, «one must circumcise» him again."
  }
